[31m-**## 🧠 System Architecture**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**The system uses a centralized IoT architecture composed of three major layers.**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**### Hardware Layer**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**The ESP32 acts as the central controller and interfaces with the sensors, motor drivers, and DC motors.**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**### Cloud Layer**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**\*\*Firebase Realtime Database\*\* provides real-time data exchange between the ESP32 and Flutter application.**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**The RTDB is organized into four major data areas:**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**```text**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**Configuration**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**Commands**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**Monitoring**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**History**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**```**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**Configuration stores operational parameters, schedules, modes, and target doses.**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**Commands are used for instant/custom feeding and on-demand sensor requests.**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**Monitoring contains current feed-stock, moisture, and PIR activity information.**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**History stores previous feeding execution records for monitoring and evaluation.**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**### Application Layer**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**The Flutter mobile application provides the user interface for monitoring, configuration, remote feeding control, and historical data.**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**Authentication and \*\*Rule-Based Access Control (RBAC)\*\* are used to restrict access to critical configuration and actuator control operations.**[m
